{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BLOCKED at the plan-review CLAIM GATE (not started; no code touched, ticket left open/unclaimed).\n\nreview-plan 6454-d06e fast-fails INDETERMINATE/exit 2 (no LLM, no attestation): 'not claimable yet: blocked by unclosed ticket(s) fea4-f98c-f1a2-4168'. Per task constraint, did NOT --force.\n\nfea4 (== 'ticket B') is its Gerrit change 1813 (commit cde01d009e). As of now 1813 is status NEW, LLM-Review +1 but Verified -1 (CI REJECTED) — not merged into origin/main (origin/main tip 42cd70b889 does not contain cde01d009e; origin/main reconcile_helpers.py still uses the raw git_adapter path). fea4 therefore correctly remains in_progress and E stays blocked until 1813's CI is fixed, 1813 merges, and fea4 closes. Resolving 1813's CI is fea4's owner's job (assignee joeoakhart@navapbc.com, worktree impl-fea4-seams), not E's.\n\nPre-work analysis completed so E can proceed immediately once fea4 lands:\n- alert_store residency DETERMINED = LOCAL SCRATCH. alert_store writes to repo_root/bridge_state/bridge_alerts (no dot), which .gitignore line 14 ('bridge_state/') ignores; the tickets branch only carries the dotted .bridge_state/* (git ls-tree origin/tickets shows bindings.json/get_rotation.json/last-pass.json/peer_confirmations.json/prev_snapshot.json/projects.json, NO bridge_alerts). So fsutil.atomic_write ALONE is correct — no publish/commit path. Only _atomic_write (called by patch_bug_filed) is converted; preserve exact bytes, 0o600 mode (mkstemp default, no chmod today), and fsync durability -> fsutil.atomic_write(path, content, permissions=0o600, fsync=True).\n- binding snapshot: route _commit_binding_store_snapshot through push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker_dir, message=..., strict=True) INSIDE the existing try/except. strict=True maps a PushDeliveryError back to the current fail-open False+alert path; clean tree -> no commit (no-op idempotency preserved). Note: the seam stages via 'git add -A' vs today's selective 5-file staging; in a normal pass only the binding files are dirty in .tickets-tracker at that point (projects.json is a rare operator write; prev_snapshot.json is written AFTER this call), so the committed set matches, and this is the sanctioned unified-lock behavior mirroring GHA commit-back. Existing subprocess-mocking tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/ (test_commit_binding_store_failure.py, test_binding_retired_commit.py, test_get_rotation_commit_heldout.py, etc.) are coupled to the raw-git command sequence and will need re-pointing at the seam-level behavior."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786814969266488001,"uuid":"1ed32ad2-52f2-4520-9c2a-1d92697c41da"}